## 5. Test data

Every test uses unique data (factory or `Date.now()`), cleans up after itself, and has no order dependence. Never depend on another student's data in the shared test environment.

```typescript
// ✅ Good
const name = `booking-${Date.now()}`;
const booking = await createBookingViaApi(request, { name });
try {
  await expect(page.getByText(name)).toBeVisible();
} finally {
  await deleteBookingViaApi(request, booking.id);
}

// ❌ Bad
await page.getByText('Yaroslav shared demo booking').click(); // another student's fixture
```

**Why:** Unique, self-owned data prevents cross-test and cross-student collisions in a shared environment.

---

## 6. Tags

Exactly one tag per `test()`: `@smoke` (every PR), `@sanity` (every push), `@regression` (full suite on manual dispatch), `@api`, `@e2e`, `@destructive` (ONLY shared/global state such as account settings both families depend on; runs `--workers=1`). Never tag `describe()`. Own-data tests are not `@destructive`. Any state-mutating test reverts in `afterEach` / `afterAll`.

```typescript
// ✅ Good
test('signs in and lands on home @smoke', async ({ page }) => {
  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Home' })).toBeVisible();
});

test('toggles org-wide setting @destructive', async ({ page }) => {
  // mutate shared setting, then revert in afterEach
});

// ❌ Bad
test.describe('bookings @regression', () => { // tag on describe
  test('creates booking @smoke @e2e', async ({ page }) => { // more than one tag
    // mutates shared settings without @destructive or revert
  });
});
```

**Why:** One tag per test keeps CI selection deterministic; `@destructive` isolates the rare shared-state cases that cannot run in parallel.

