## 7. Test data sources

Use `test-data/factories/` (Faker + `Date.now()`) for builders, static invalid sets in `test-data/*.ts`, secrets and URLs from `process.env`, and repeated strings in enums (e.g. `test-data/routes.ts`).

```typescript
// ✅ Good
import { buildUser } from '../test-data/factories/user.factory';
import { Routes } from '../test-data/routes';

const user = buildUser();
await page.goto(Routes.login);
await page.getByLabel('Email').fill(process.env.USER_EMAIL!);

// ❌ Bad
await page.goto('/login');
await page.getByLabel('Email').fill('fixed.user@example.com');
const payload = { name: 'Ada', email: 'ada@example.com' }; // inline magic strings
```

**Why:** Central factories and enums remove duplication and keep secrets and environment URLs out of specs.

