## 8. API

Use the `request` fixture for setup, teardown, and contract checks. Never build prerequisite data through the UI when an API exists.

```typescript
// ✅ Good
test('shows an existing booking @api', async ({ page, request }) => {
  const booking = await createBookingViaApi(request, buildBooking());
  await page.goto(`/bookings/${booking.id}`);
  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: booking.name })).toBeVisible();
  await deleteBookingViaApi(request, booking.id);
});

// ❌ Bad
test('shows an existing booking @e2e', async ({ page }) => {
  // click through the whole create-booking UI just to seed state for a read assertion
});
```

**Why:** API seeding is faster and less flake-prone than UI setup for data the test is not validating.

