## 10. Accessibility

Run an `@axe-core/playwright` scan with `wcag2a` / `wcag2aa` on key pages plus a keyboard-operability check. Working `getByRole(…, { name })` locators prove accessible names.

```typescript
// ✅ Good
const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page }).withTags(['wcag2a', 'wcag2aa']).analyze();
expect(results.violations).toEqual([]);
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Save' }).focus();
await page.keyboard.press('Enter');

// ❌ Bad
await page.locator('.btn-primary').click(); // no accessible name; no axe or keyboard coverage
```

**Why:** Axe catches systematic WCAG issues; role-by-name locators double as a living check that controls expose names.

