## 11. Assertions

Prefer web-first assertions. Use `expect.soft` for multi-check reports. Use `toHaveScreenshot` only with dynamic regions masked.

```typescript
// ✅ Good
await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Bookings' })).toBeVisible();
await expect.soft(page.getByText('Upcoming')).toBeVisible();
await expect.soft(page.getByText('Past')).toBeVisible();
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot('bookings.png', {
  mask: [page.getByTestId('clock'), page.getByTestId('avatar')],
});

// ❌ Bad
expect(await page.getByText('Upcoming').textContent()).toBe('Upcoming');
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot('bookings.png'); // unmasked dynamic regions
```

**Why:** Soft asserts collect multiple failures in one run; masking keeps screenshots deterministic when clocks and avatars change.

---

## 12. Anti-flake

Retries in CI only; full isolation; `page.clock` for time (availability and calendars depend on "now"); pinned locale and timezone; trace on first retry. Raising `retries: 5` or forcing `workers: 1` is not a fix (except `@destructive` as defined above).

```typescript
// ✅ Good
await page.clock.setFixedTime(new Date('2026-09-29T12:00:00-04:00'));
// playwright.config: retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0, locale/timezone pinned, trace: 'on-first-retry'

// ❌ Bad
// playwright.config: retries: 5, workers: 1  // papering over races
await page.waitForTimeout(5000);
```

**Why:** Flakes are isolation, timing, or env drift; more retries hide the bug instead of removing the race.

---

## Refusals (hard stops)

These are conflicts the agent raises — not preferences it can be talked out of:

- Never weaken or delete an assertion to pass.
- Never heal a real bug.
- Never replace a role locator with CSS/XPath.
- Never use `waitForTimeout`, a hardcoded credential, or the `any` type.
